1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,600
On Slide 20, let us look at the physical silicon powering this intelligence: Google's TPU v8.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,650
Many students ask us: "Can't we just run these swarms on regular graphics cards?"

3
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:26,800
Traditional GPUs are great for gaming and general graphics, but Google TPU v8 silicon is purpose-built exclusively for transformer neural network matrices.

4
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:38,640
TPU v8 pods utilize Optical Circuit Switching (OCS). That means hundreds of TPU chips communicate with each other using beams of light with virtually zero latency!

5
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:47,740
That hardware foundation is what makes multi-agent swarm collaboration possible at scale without astronomical cloud bills.

